# The integration image (infra/docker/integration/Dockerfile) has no COPY or ADD
# - it only installs a toolchain, and the repo arrives at runtime as a volume
# mount. So nothing here needs a build context at all, but docker still uploads
# one: without this file that is the whole working tree, including a target/
# directory that reaches tens of gigabytes. Ignoring everything keeps the upload
# at a few kilobytes.
*
